/*
Problem: Count Nodes in Binary Tree

-----------------------------------------------------

Problem Statement

Given the root of a binary tree,
count the total number of nodes.

-----------------------------------------------------

Pattern Used & Why

Pattern: DFS (Recursion)

Why:
- Total nodes = left subtree + right subtree + current node
- Recursively count all nodes

-----------------------------------------------------

Key Idea

- Count = left count + right count + 1

-----------------------------------------------------

Algorithm / Process

1. If root is null → return 0
2. Count nodes in left subtree
3. Count nodes in right subtree
4. Return left + right + 1

-----------------------------------------------------

Code
*/

class Solution {

    int countNodes(Node root) {

        // base case
        if (root == null) return 0;

        int left = countNodes(root.left);
        int right = countNodes(root.right);

        return left + right + 1;
    }
}

/*
-----------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity
O(n)

-----------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity
O(n)

-----------------------------------------------------

Example

Input:
    1
   / \
  2   3
 /
4

Output:
4

-----------------------------------------------------

Short Explanation

Count nodes of left subtree + right subtree + current node.
*/

-----------------------------------------------------

// Definition for Node
class Node {
    int data;
    Node left;
    Node right;

    Node(int val) {
        this.data = val;
        this.left = null;
        this.right = null;
    }
}
